Package: mount-manager
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, util-linux, gvfs-backends, cifs-utils, sudo | policykit-1
Recommends: sshfs, nfs-common, smbclient, davfs2, avahi-utils, libsecret-tools, libglib2.0-bin, policykit-1, psmisc
Suggests: gnome-keyring, rclone
Description: manage mounted external paths (SMB, NFS, SFTP, WebDAV, FTP, disks)
 Mount Manager is a GTK4/libadwaita application that keeps every mounted
 external path in one place. It shows what is currently mounted, unmounts
 busy or stale filesystems, and connects new shares through a form instead
 of a terminal.
 .
 Supported protocols: SMB/CIFS (Windows shares, Samba, NAS), NFS v3/v4,
 SSHFS/SFTP, WebDAV over HTTP(S), FTP, local block devices (USB sticks, SD
 cards, external disks) and bind mounts. Anything else can be mounted with
 the "custom" filesystem type.
 .
 Features: mDNS/Avahi network browsing, share/export listing, connection
 testing, saved shares with optional /etc/fstab persistence (always with a
 backup), keyring password storage, mounting without admin rights through
 GVFS/FUSE, and a full command line interface for scripts.
 .
 Administrator rights are obtained through polkit (pkexec) with a sudo
 fallback that asks for the password inside the application, so it also works
 in containers that have no authentication agent.
